From: Remy <remy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: PON: refuse unrepresentable targets and prove arbiter offsets against FDT spans

Correction to 0040 answering the monitor review (044647e).
(1) Malformed-address aliasing: ppid() masks to 12 bits and
ext_cmd() masks the address, so sid=16 and reg=0x10088f both
silently aliased sid 0 / reg 0x088f and returned Ok. New
validate_target() (SID_MAX=0xF, SPMI_REG_MAX=0xFFFF) is the
first statement of both transaction entry points; the probe
range-checks the FDT slave ID and computes the reason
register with checked_add + the same bound.
(2) Unproved MMIO bounds: the probe now preserves every FDT
region span, refuses misaligned or wrapping bases, and the
kernel calls the new set_reason_with_bus_bounded(): target
validation, core-span header check, version gate, APID
discovery capped by the core/cnfg spans, and the chosen
APID's channel windows proven against the obsrvr/chnls spans
- all before the first channel access. Host tests 26/26:
the 14 originals, the reviewer's two controls verbatim
(RED on 0040, GREEN here), and the span-refusal cases, each
asserting an empty write trace on refusal.

